   :circumstances ["You were raised in the next parish but one, the eldest of a wheelwright's crowded children, and came to Claudeworth at three-and-twenty with a box of books, a good opinion of yourself and no acquaintance in the place." "You write every week to a widowed aunt at Wendover who kept you through your mother's long illness, and you have twice petitioned the Post Office over the late mail-bags and twice been refused, which you have not forgotten."]
