   :circumstances ["You came to Claudeworth years ago from a stocking-knitting village in Leicestershire, where your father and brothers worked the frames and you were bound apprentice to a barber in the nearest market town; the loom never suited your hands or your patience." "A widowed sister still in Leicestershire writes to you monthly, and you keep her letters in a tin by the grate. You have no kin here, and take your dinner alone."]
