   :circumstances ["Second son of a Belfast chandler; the shop by the quay passed to his elder brother, who writes twice a year of the linen trade and of debts, and whose letters you answer by return and at length." "Came to Hollin by way of a northern seminary and a year as chaplain to a garrison, and still sends what little he can spare to a sister widowed young in Antrim, and keeps up a correspondence with two former soldiers who once made their confessions to him."]
   :appearance "A lean man of about thirty-five, of middling height, with a thin, lined face and quick wary eyes; his dark hair is cropped short and greying at the temples, and his hands are broad for a monk's. He wears a plain black habit, somewhat rubbed at the cuffs, and carries himself with a slight stoop, watchful and attentive."
