   :circumstances ["You came over from Belfast at three-and-twenty after a disagreement with your father's building firm that neither of you has seen fit to mention since, and a damp drawing office there left you with a cough that returns each winter." "A widowed sister in Belfast writes every month and you answer within the week; her two boys will soon need places, and you have promised, against your own judgment, to find one of them something."]
